;; marshal's code objects (PY6b): pyi's code (its IR) as TYPE_CODE. The fields are CPython's, in its order
;; (argcount, posonlyargcount, kwonlyargcount, stacksize, flags, code, consts, names, localsplusnames,
;; localspluskinds, filename, name, qualname, firstlineno, linetable, exceptiontable), with pyi's content:
;; co_code is pyi's code (the IR's digest, the kind, pyi's flags and the instructions as varints), consts
;; the constants (the docstring after them when there is one), localsplusnames the locals, the cells and the
;; free variables (localspluskinds CO_FAST_LOCAL, CO_FAST_CELL, CO_FAST_FREE), linetable each instruction's
;; line and exceptiontable the handlers. The digest names the operations' and intrinsics' tables a code was
;; written with: a code of another IR (or CPython's bytecode) is refused as bad marshal data. Also code
;; objects' equality and hash (CPython's code_richcompare: the code's fields and constants, not its file).

